Cuba the first of what would eventually be three boxing titles in Rio.\nLa Cruz was hit by a bullet above his left hip in his home town of Camaguey in 2014 while leaving a restaurant.\n" [:a {:href "/athletes/133825"} "Mathieu Bauderlique"] " of France and " [:a {:href "/athletes/133991"} "Joshua Buatsi"] " of Great Britain won the bronze medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123514"} "Julio César la Cruz"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CUB"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CUB.png"}] "CUB"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126824"} "Adilbek Niyazymbetov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KAZ"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KAZ.png"}] "KAZ"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133825"} "Mathieu Bauderlique"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133991"} "Joshua Buatsi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/132788"} "Michel Borges"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countrie